{
  "comment": [
    "Which HideTheme values the design canvas carries, and under what name.",
    "",
    "`mapped` is the generator's territory: the generator writes each of these into",
    "design/hide.pen and the check fails when one drifts. Every other variable in that",
    "file is the canvas's own and is never touched - the --asbuilt-* family that names",
    "the off-scale numbers the app writes directly, the --proposed-* family the",
    "reconciliation needs, and the derived tints pen cannot compute.",
    "",
    "`unmapped` is the rest of HideTheme, with the reason it stays out. It exists so the",
    "check can refuse a new HideTheme constant that is in neither list: silence is how a",
    "token reaches the shell without ever reaching the design.",
    "",
    "A Swift path is dot-separated from HideTheme; `lanes.0` indexes an array literal."
  ],
